        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "where $p(k)$ is the prior of the model $k$, and $p(\\boldsymbol{\\theta}_{k}|k)$ is the prior of parameters $\\boldsymbol{\\theta}_{k}$ in this model. In our case, the parameters to be estimated are encoded in the covariance matrix $C(f)$. The likelihood $p(s|k,\\boldsymbol{\\theta}_{k})$ takes the form",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                719,
                1127,
                768
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    103.0,
                    719.0
                ],
                [
                    1127.0,
                    719.0
                ],
                [
                    1127.0,
                    768.0
                ],
                [
                    103.0,
                    768.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "display_formula",
            "block_content": " $$ \\begin{align*}\\ln p(s|C)=&-\\sum_{i,f}\\left[\\det(C_{i}(f))+s_{i}^\\dagger(f)C_{i}^{-1}(f)s_{i}(f)\\right],\\\\s_{i}(f)=&\\left[A_{i}(f)\\ E_{i}(f)\\ T_{i}(f)\\right]^{T},\\end{align*} $$ ",
            "block_bbox": [
